# AWS Kinesis Data Firehose to S3 Pipeline (Terraform)

This Terraform configuration provisions a streaming data ingestion pipeline using **Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose** to deliver records into an **Amazon S3** bucket with automated newline record delimiting.

## Overview

- **S3 Bucket (`xfusion-stream-bucket-150002905`)**: Destination storage for incoming Firehose delivery batches.
- **IAM Role (`firehose-sts-role`) & Policy**: Allows `firehose.amazonaws.com` to assume the role via STS (`sts:AssumeRole`) and write objects to the target S3 bucket.
- **Kinesis Data Firehose (`xfusion-firehose-stream`)**:
  - Uses `extended_s3` destination configuration.
  - Buffers incoming data up to **5 MB** or **300 seconds**, whichever comes first.
  - Appends a newline delimiter (`\n`) after each record using `AppendDelimiterToRecord`.
  - Waits for IAM policy attachment via `depends_on`.

